<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Partial Info.plist, merged with the keys Xcode generates from the target's
	  INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES).

	  UIBackgroundModes lives here because INFOPLIST_KEY_UIBackgroundModes does NOT work:
	  Xcode only maps an allowlist of known INFOPLIST_KEY_* settings into the generated
	  plist, and array-valued UIBackgroundModes is not one of them. The build setting is
	  accepted without error and silently produces no key, which would leave interval cues
	  dying the moment the screen locks — with nothing in the build log to say so.

	  "audio" is required so the interval timer and its cues keep running while the phone is
	  locked or the app is backgrounded (spec §9.4, §23). AudioCueEngine holds the session
	  open with a silent looping player for exactly this reason.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
		<string>workout-processing</string>
	</array>
	<!--
	  "workout-processing" (added 2026-09-25, watch link step 1): the watch mirrors its
	  HKWorkoutSession to this app, and HealthKit may launch or wake the app in the background to
	  hand the session over (HKHealthStore.workoutSessionMirroringStartHandler). Declared so the
	  phone can receive it while locked. Whether the phone strictly needs it has NOT been measured.
	-->


	<!--
	  Required for ActivityKit. Like UIBackgroundModes there is no working
	  INFOPLIST_KEY_ equivalent, so it lives here where it demonstrably lands in the
	  built app. Without it Activity.request throws at runtime and the Lock Screen
	  card silently never appears.
	-->
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
	<true/>

	<!--
	  Declares that this app updates its Live Activity at a moderate rate (roughly once
	  per interval transition).

	  DOES NOT FIX THE BACKGROUND-UPDATE BUG, and was added while testing the theory that
	  it would. Recorded here so nobody re-runs that experiment: with this key present and
	  `ActivityAuthorizationInfo.frequentPushesEnabled` reporting **true**, an instrumented
	  device run on 2026-08-07 still had every background `Activity.update` silently
	  discarded. iOS applies the update only while the app is in the foreground. See
	  docs/CUE_FEASIBILITY_TEST.md, Test 3, for the three-run evidence.

	  Kept because the declaration is accurate, not because it changed any behaviour.
	-->
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivitiesFrequentUpdates</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
